# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Windows shell scripts must keep CRLF in the working tree, otherwise a checkout
# that later lands on a Windows box produces a .bat cmd.exe can mis-parse around
# labels and goto.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# NOTE: PowerShell scripts are deliberately NOT listed here.
#   * smoke-test.ps1 contains Chinese string literals and therefore carries a
#     UTF-8 BOM, because Windows PowerShell 5.1 decodes .ps1 files using the
#     ANSI code page when no BOM is present - that mangles the literals and can
#     even make the file unparseable.
#   * package-release.ps1, build-release.ps1 and security-test.ps1 are kept
#     pure ASCII on purpose so they decode identically in every code page.
#   * Do NOT add `working-tree-encoding=UTF-8` for these: git documents it as
#     unnecessary and harmful for files that are already UTF-8, and it can
#     mangle the BOM as well as leave files perpetually showing as modified.
# Keep *.ps1 to plain line-ending normalization (already implied by text=auto).

# Keep binary assets untouched (text=auto would normally detect these anyway;
# being explicit prevents an unlucky heuristic from corrupting them).
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.zip   binary
*.exe   binary
